WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.890
Before deployment, detections should be tested whenever practical.

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:08.471
Testing helps confirm that the detection logic works as intended and that the required telemetry exists.

00:00:08.471 --> 00:00:11.262
Validation also checks whether alert details are useful.

00:00:11.262 --> 00:00:15.098
Analysts need enough context to understand what happened, why it matters,

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:16.842
and what should happen next.

00:00:16.842 --> 00:00:20.330
Testing may reveal missing fields, overly broad conditions, excessive noise,

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:23.121
or assumptions that do not match the environment.

00:00:23.121 --> 00:00:26.260
These findings are useful because they prevent avoidable disruption.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:30.446
Detection testing is not about proving a rule will be perfect forever.

00:00:30.446 --> 00:00:34.980
It is about building confidence that the detection is ready for operational use.
